# Triaged Trivy IaC findings — accepted risks with justification.
# Reviewed: each entry is a deliberate architecture decision, not an oversight.
# Anything NOT listed here is expected to be fixed (the CI gate fails on it).
# Re-review on any change to networking, the ALB, or the state backend.

# AWS-0054 (CRITICAL) ALB listener uses HTTP, not HTTPS.
#   Accepted: this is the DEV-ONLY listener (count=0 when a cert is set). prod
#   sets certificate_arn -> the HTTPS listener is used and HTTP redirects. So
#   HTTPS IS enforced everywhere a cert exists; dev runs HTTP by design.
AWS-0054

# AWS-0104 (CRITICAL) Security group allows unrestricted egress (0.0.0.0/0).
#   Accepted: tasks need outbound to ECR, AWS APIs, and vendor endpoints.
#   Locking egress to specific CIDRs/prefix-lists is a separate hardening effort.
AWS-0104

# AWS-0053 (HIGH) Load balancer is exposed publicly.
#   Accepted: this IS the public, internet-facing scoring API. Intentional.
AWS-0053

# AWS-0132 (HIGH) S3 bucket not encrypted with a customer-managed KMS key.
#   Accepted: state buckets use AWS-managed KMS (aws:kms). Adequate for this
#   project; a CMK adds key rotation/policy overhead without a requirement.
AWS-0132

# AWS-0164 (HIGH) Subnet assigns public IPs.
#   Accepted: the PUBLIC subnets host the ALB and NAT gateway by design. App
#   tasks run in PRIVATE subnets with no public IPs.
AWS-0164

# AWS-0024 (MEDIUM) Point-in-time recovery not enabled.
#   Accepted: applies to the Terraform lock table (ephemeral lock rows). The
#   audit table — the actual system of record — DOES enable PITR.
AWS-0024

# AWS-0178 (MEDIUM) VPC has no flow logs.
#   FOLLOW-UP (accepted for now): VPC Flow Logs -> CloudWatch is a worthwhile
#   add for network forensics; tracked as a future hardening task.
AWS-0178
